      "player": "Qwen3L Worrier",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Oh no — I’m down to six cards now, and I have to put one on the bottom. Which one do I cut?\n\
\n\
My new hand is:\n\
- Undercity Informer\n\
- Bridge from Below\n\
- Reanimate\n\
- Thassa’s Oracle\n\
- Thoughtseize\n\
- Elvish Spirit Guide\n\
- Lotus Petal\n\
\n\
I need to pick one to bottom. This is brutal.\n\
\n\
Let’s think.\n\
\n\
I’m playing a Reanimator/Thassa’s Oracle combo deck. The way it wins is by either Reanimating a creature and recurring Bridge from Below triggers, or by decking the opponent with Thassa’s Oracle.\n\
\n\
Key pieces:\n\
- Reanimate: reanimates a creature from graveyard.\n\
- Bridge from Below: creates zombie tokens when a creature is buried or sacrificed — *and* can be used to trigger the loop.\n\
- Thassa’s Oracle: if your library is empty, you win.\n\
- Thoughtseize: discard outlet and card advantage.\n\
- Elvish Spirit Guide and Lotus Petal: mana dorks and acceleration.\n\
\n\
Undercity Informer can help dig, but it’s slow.\n\
\n\
Now, which one is the least critical?\n\
\n\
Bridge from Below is very important — it’s the engine for the zombie token loop. Without it, I can’t generate infinite zombies.\n\
\n\
Reanimate is essential — I can’t reanimate without it.\n\
\n\
Thassa’s Oracle is my alternate win condition — absolutely vital.\n\
\n\
Thoughtseize is a great discard outlet, hand read, and mana source via triggering Threshold later.\n\
\n\
Elvish Spirit Guide and Lotus Petal are mana accelerators — both are strong, but I already have one of each.\n\
\n\
I have to cut one. If I lose one mana dork, I still have the other. But if I lose either Reanimate or Bridge, I’m probably dead in the water.\n\
\n\
Wait — I also have Undercity Informer. It’s nice, but not essential.\n\
\n\
But let’s compare:\n\
\n\
- Cutting Elvish Spirit Guide: I’d still have Lotus Petal, which is free and can make any color. But ESG can be exiled for G, which might help with casting Reanimate or setting up Oracle.\n\
\n\
- Cutting Lotus Petal: same — I’d still have ESG, and it’s also free.\n\
\n\
But Lotus Petal can make any color, while ESG only makes green — which I might not even need.\n\
\n\
Wait, but in this deck, green is only for Elvish Spirit Guide itself and maybe Balustrade Spy. But I didn’t draw any of those.\n\
\n\
Thassa’s Oracle needs to be cast or put into play, but it doesn’t require green.\n\
\n\
Reanimate is black.\n\
\n\
Thoughtseize is black.\n\
\n\
Bridge and Undercity are colorless or black.\n\
\n\
So green isn’t really needed — but ESG can be exiled for mana, so it’s still useful.\n\
\n\
However, Lotus Petal is better because it can add *any* color and costs nothing to use.\n\
\n\
So maybe Elvish Spirit Guide is the weakest link? I have another green card, but I don’t need green.\n\
\n\
Undercity Informer is *also* not great — it mills, but slowly.\n\
\n\
But if I’m going for Oracle, I want to empty my library fast. So Undercity Informer could help, but I’d need to sacrifice creatures.\n\
\n\
But with Reanimate, I can get multiple bodies back to trigger Bridge.\n\
\n\
Bridge from Below triggers when creatures go to graveyard from anywhere — so Reanimating a creature to sack it can trigger Bridge.\n\
\n\
But I need something to trigger it.\n\
\n\
Thoughtseize helps by letting me pitch a card to pay for Reanimate and work on Threshold.\n\
\n\
But here’s the thing: I *have* to keep Thassa’s Oracle, Reanimate, and Bridge. They’re core.\n\
\n\
Between Lotus Petal, Elvish Spirit Guide, Thoughtseize, and Undercity Informer — I can afford to lose one.\n\
\n\
Thoughtseize is great utility — hand disruption, cost reducer, and it can help fill the graveyard.\n\
\n\
Lotus Petal is the best mana accelerator.\n\
\n\
Elvish Spirit Guide is good, but only one color.\n\
\n\
Undercity Informer is slow.\n\
\n\
So probably Undercity Informer is the least impactful? But wait — if I want to mill myself fast for Oracle, Undercity Informer can help by sacrificing things to mill.\n\
\n\
But I can also use other creatures — but I don’t have any body cards.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, maybe I should bottom Lotus Petal? It’s fragile — gets countered, and I have ESG as backup.\n\
\n\
But Lotus Petal can make any color, which is huge.\n\
\n\
ESG only makes green — which I don’t need.\n\
\n\
But I can exile ESG for mana, same as playing it.\n\
\n\
Hmm.\n\
\n\
Wait — here’s a thought: if I *don’t* need green, then ESG’s mana ability is useless, but I can still exile it for {G} to help pay for spells.\n\
\n\
But if I exile it, I get {G}, but I still need black for Reanimate and Thoughtseize.\n\
\n\
Lotus Petal can do {B}, which is critical.\n\
\n\
So Lotus Petal is better because it can produce black.\n\
\n\
ESG produces green, which I don’t need.\n\
\n\
So Elvish Spirit Guide is actually *weaker* than Lotus Petal in this deck.\n\
\n\
Therefore, Elvish Spirit Guide is the best card to bottom.\n\
\n\
I’ll put Elvish Spirit Guide on the bottom.\n\
\n\
It hurts — I’m cutting a mana source — but at least I keep the more flexible one.\n\
\n\
So I’ll choose p8 — Elvish Spirit Guide.\n\
\n\
