  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player is holding the Doomsday-style combo of Undercity Informer + Bridge from Below + Narcomoeba + Thassa's Oracle, which can win the game. Dark Ritual is essential mana to cast the combo pieces (Undercity Informer costs 2B, and they need mana to activate it). With two Dark Rituals, they can generate BBB + BBB = 6 black mana, which is enough to cast Undercity Informer (2B) and have mana left for activations. Discarding one Dark Ritual significantly weakens the combo's mana availability. Simian Spirit Guide only provides R mana which is largely irrelevant to the combo plan (all combo pieces need black or colorless mana). Additionally, with Karn + Mycosynth Lattice on the opponent's board, activated abilities of the player's artifacts can't be activated — and since Mycosynth Lattice makes all permanents artifacts, this locks out many options. The player needs to combo off quickly before the lock tightens. Discarding Simian Spirit Guide (which provides off-color mana of minimal use) would have been correct, preserving both Dark Rituals for the combo turn.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Dark Ritual",
      "better_line": "Discard Simian Spirit Guide, which only provides red mana that doesn't contribute to the BBB-heavy combo plan. Keeping both Dark Rituals maximizes the chance of comboing off with Undercity Informer + Bridge from Below + Narcomoeba + Thassa's Oracle.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 103,
      "player": "Qwen3L Worrier",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Animating Mycosynth Lattice into a creature makes the key lock piece vulnerable to creature removal. With Karn + Mycosynth Lattice, the opponent literally cannot activate any abilities (including tapping lands for mana) since all permanents are artifacts and Karn prevents opponents from activating artifact abilities. This is a complete hard lock. Making the Lattice a creature risks the opponent finding creature removal to break the lock.",
      "action_taken": "Animated Mycosynth Lattice into a 6/6 creature with Karn's +1",
      "better_line": "Choose no target for Karn's +1 (it says 'up to one'), keeping Mycosynth Lattice safe as a noncreature artifact and maintaining the unbreakable Karn+Lattice lock while winning slowly with Glaring Fleshraker attacks.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 110,
      "player": "Opus Valley",
      "decision_index": 20,
    }
  ],
